# bench6-probe.env — the one-VM GCE probe (benchmark-probe.sh all; design section 6).
# Parsed by launch.sh, never sourced: KEY=value lines only (README.md, "Env files").
# Fill the run id at gate G0 (a fresh rYYYYMMDD-HHMM, not a fleet run's) and commit the file, or fill a
# copy outside benchmark/ and launch with that copy.

BENCH_RUN_ID=<run-id>

# The probe binary built by benchmark/tools/build-probe-bin.sh (build-info.txt beside it).
LAUNCH_PROBE_BIN=benchmark/work/probe-bin/mdbx-writeback-probe
# The arms to run (benchmark-probe.sh --arms); unset = all of them. `core` is the short run.
# LAUNCH_PROBE_ARMS=core
# The devices (benchmark-probe.sh --disks); unset = hyperdisk, the fleet's shape and boot disk. `both` runs
# each arm on the boot disk and on a local NVMe SSD of a c3-standard-8-lssd; pair it with the subset
# LAUNCH_PROBE_ARMS=g1-node,g5,g8-nowritemap (launch/README.md, "The probe").
# LAUNCH_PROBE_DISKS=both

# The boot image of the fleet the probe stands in for, pinned.
BENCH_NODE_BOOT_IMAGE=projects/ubuntu-os-cloud/global/images/ubuntu-2404-noble-amd64-v20261105
